In article <13615@bloom-beacon.MIT.EDU> (Dave Policar) writes:

>>   |--------
>>   |@^......  <- You digging
>>   |^d.....   <- Your pet in a pit (will follow you)
>>   |@.......  <- Standing shopkeeper watching you robbering the shop
>
>  I tried this recently, after filling the entire shop with pits for good 
> measure, and got the message "The shopkeeper leaps and grabs your pack!"
> so it isn't foolproof (though I'd imagine it's rare).

Try this instead:

     |--------
    ^+@.......  <- You about to jump into your private chute
     |.%.....   <- Dead pet you got tired of bumping into
     |@.......  <- Shopkeeper about to lose his shirt

On a prior visit, you "case" the joint and create a new exit.  Just outside
you dig a trapdoor, fall through and work your way back to the shop.  On your
return, you should have little trouble picking up all the valuables and making
a clean getaway.  Only one thing can possibly go wrong.  Sometimes you escape
your own trapdoor!  It can be quite embarrassing standing there unable to fall,
while the Kops or shopkeeper administer "justice".

V3.0 is an interesting game, although my previous "hack and slash" style of
play doesn't suit it well.  There's a formidable learning curve for beginners.
I feel sorry for anyone who hadn't already mastered the previous version.  Is
there such a thing as a high-survivability armor class, or do you never reach
the point where you can take on any monster in hand to hand combat?

